discussion_timeline.body:
[aeron-cluster/src/main/java/io/aeron/cluster/ConsensusModuleAgent.java] Everywhere else the following pattern is used:
```java
if (clusterSessionId >= nextSessionId)
{
    nextSessionId = clusterSessionId + 1;
}
```
And the same should be done here for `nextCommittedSessionId`.

[aeron-system-tests/src/test/java/io/aeron/cluster/ClusterTest.java] Instead of calling `TestClutser#connectClient` we should create a standalone `AeronCluster` instance. Something like this:
```java
// Original client - should always be allowed
final AeronCluster client = connectClient();

final AeronCluster.Context clientContext = new AeronCluster.Context()
    .aeronDirectoryName(client.context().aeronDirectoryName())
    .aeron(client.context().aeron())
    .ingressChannel(client.context().ingressChannel())
    .ingressStreamId(555)
    .isIngressExclusive(true)
    .egressChannel(client.context().egressChannel())
    .egressStreamId(777)
    .ingressEndpoints(client.context().ingressEndpoints());

// Another session -> also OK
final AeronCluster client2 = AeronCluster.connect(clientContext.clone());

// Any further connections are rejected
assertThrowsExactly(AuthenticationException.class, () -> AeronCluster.connect(clientContext.clone()));
```

@mikeb01 The error translation happens in the `aeron_driver_conductor_on_command`:
```c
int os_errno = aeron_errcode();
int code = os_errno < 0 ? -os_errno : AERON_ERROR_CODE_GENERIC_ERROR;
aeron_driver_conductor_on_error(conductor, code, aeron_errmsg(), strlen(aeron_errmsg()), correlation_id);
aeron_driver_conductor_log_error(conductor);
```
and because the check emits `-AERON_ERROR_CODE_STORAGE_SPACE` it will come out as `AERON_ERROR_CODE_STORAGE_SPACE`.

I was considering to convert the raw `ENOSPC` into the `AERON_ERROR_CODE_STORAGE_SPACE` instead. But that would be different from all other custom errors codes we emit and also will not match Java which only handle insufficient space errors for the log files.

Thanks for the test I'll add it to the PR.
